<title>USA: SEC halts Twenty First Century trading.</title>
<headline>SEC halts Twenty First Century trading.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Securities and Exchange Commission said Thursday it had ordered the temporary suspension of trading in the stock of Las Vegas-based Twenty First Century Health Inc until March 12.</p>
<p>The commission said it ordered the suspension because of questions raised about the adequacy and accuracy of certain information publicly disseminated by the company.</p>
<p>The suspension began at 0900 EST/1400 GMT today and will end at 2359 EST March 12 (0459 GMT March 13), the agency said.</p>
</text>
